target/
.git/
.github/
docs/
.claude/
.env
.env.*
*.md
!README.md

# Key material must never enter the build context. `tests/data/test_idp_key.pem`
# is one today: harmless in itself (a throwaway IdP key in a public repo, and
# the runtime stage copies only the binary), but `COPY . .` pulled it into the
# builder layer, and `cache-to: type=gha` exports those layers. The binary
# embeds exactly one external file — `config/example.yaml` — so nothing here is
# reachable from `cargo build --release`. Deny by extension, not by path, so the
# next key added anywhere is covered without anyone remembering this file.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.crt

# The Docusaurus site is ~400 MB with node_modules and is never part of the
# binary. Left in, it dominated the build context and made a docs-only push
# invalidate the `COPY . .` layer, forcing a cold release rebuild.
website/

# Local tooling state — same reasoning: context weight and spurious cache busts.
tmp/
.codegraph/
.claude-task-master/

# The planner stage generates this itself. A `cargo chef prepare` run in the
# working tree would otherwise ship a stale copy in the build context, busting
# the planner's `COPY . .` layer on a file the build immediately overwrites.
recipe.json
